vided by 18 is 9. Therefore, we have:\n\n\\[ 142857 \\equiv 9 \\pmod{18} \\]\n\nSo, the integer \\( n \\) that satisfies \\( 0 \\le n < 18 \\) and \\( n \\equiv 142857 \\pmod{18} \\) is \\( n = 9 \\).\n\nThe final answer is:\n\n\\[ \\boxed{9} \\]"},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{9}","correct":true,"format":"boxed","parseable":true},"id":"number_theory:31"}
